(1)   36/   16348 :                     		; This check doesn't really work: it's possible for an object to be
(1)   37/   16348 :                     		; loaded into the parent's slot before this object can check if the
(1)   38/   16348 :                     		; slot is empty. In fact, it will always be immediately occupied by
(1)   39/   16348 :                     		; the explosion object. This defect causes the flame to linger for a
(1)   40/   16348 :                     		; while after the Buzzer is destroyed. A better way to do this check
(1)   41/   16348 :                     		; would be to check if the ID is equal to 'id_Obj4B'.
