(1) 1198/   71F50 :                     ; Unused RAM addresses for FM and PSG channel variables used by the Special SFX
(1) 1199/   71F50 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1) 1200/   71F50 :                     ; The first block would have been used for overriding the music tracks
(1) 1201/   71F50 :                     ; as they have a lower priority, just as they are in Sound_PlaySFX
(1) 1202/   71F50 :                     ; The third block would be used to set up the Special SFX
(1) 1203/   71F50 :                     ; The second block, however, is for the SFX tracks, which have a higher priority
(1) 1204/   71F50 :                     ; and would be checked for if they're currently playing
(1) 1205/   71F50 :                     ; If they are, then the third block would be used again, this time to mark
(1) 1206/   71F50 :                     ; the new tracks as 'currently playing'
(1) 1207/   71F50 :                     
(1) 1208/   71F50 :                     ; These were actually used in Moonwalker's driver (and other SMPS 68k Type 1a drivers)
(1) 1209/   71F50 :                     
